%I A400179 #9 Oct 02 2026 22:27:34
%S A400179 0,1,2,2,1,2,3,3,2,1,2,3,3,3,3,2,1,2,3,3,2,2,3,3,2,1,2,3,3,2,3,3,2,3,
%T A400179 3,2,1,2,3,3,2,3,4,4,3,2,3,3,2,1,2,3,3,2,3,4,4,4,4,3,2,3,3,2,1,2,3,3,
%U A400179 2,3,4,4,3,3,4,4,3,2,3,3,2,1,2,3,3,2,3,4,4,3,2,2,3,4,4,3,2,3,3,2,1
%N A400179 a(n) = number of iterations of the map n -> A053188(n) needed to reach 0, starting from n.
%C A400179 a(n) = 0 iff n = 0; a(n) = 1 iff n is a positive perfect square.
%C A400179 The smallest n with a(n) = t is A000058(t-1) - 1, where A000058 is Sylvester's sequence; equivalently, this minimal witness m(t) satisfies m(1) = 1, m(t) = m(t-1)*(m(t-1)+1).
%C A400179 Since A000058 grows doubly exponentially, a(n) = O(log log n): a(n) <= 6 for all n < 3263443, and a(n) <= 7 for all n < 10650056950807.
%C A400179 This sequence is not periodic: a(n) is unbounded, since a(n) = t is first attained at n = A000058(t-1) - 1, and A000058 (Sylvester's sequence) is unbounded.
%F A400179 a(0) = 0; a(n) = 1 + a(A053188(n)) for n > 0.
%e A400179 a(6) = 3: 6 -> A053188(6) = 2 -> A053188(2) = 1 -> A053188(1) = 0 (three steps: 6, 2, 1, 0).
%e A400179 a(42) = 4: 42 -> 6 -> 2 -> 1 -> 0.
%o A400179 (PARI) a(n) = my(k=0); while(n>0, n = abs((floor(sqrt(n)+1/2))^2 - n); k++); k
%Y A400179 Cf. A053188, A000058.
%K A400179 nonn,new
%O A400179 0,3
%A A400179 _Yves Debeuret_, Sep 20 2026
